# CS509 Assignment 4 — Individual Task
Vertex Coloring (Graph Coloring) + PageRank

## Layout

```
Assignment_4/
├── include/            csr.h, vertex_coloring.h, pagerank.h
├── src/                 vertex_coloring.cpp, pagerank.cpp
├── tools/               generate_color_graph.cpp, generate_pagerank_graph.cpp
├── tests/               color, pagerank
└── README.md
```


## Build

```bash
g++ -O2 -std=c++17 -Iinclude  src/vertex_coloring.cpp \
    src/pagerank.cpp tools/wrapper.cpp -o wrapper.exe
```

Generators (optional, only needed to regenerate/resize test data):

```bash
g++ -O2 -std=c++17 tools/generate_color_graph.cpp    -o gen_color.exe
g++ -O2 -std=c++17 tools/generate_pagerank_graph.cpp -o gen_pagerank.exe
# ./gen_color.exe    <V> <E> <output_path> [seed]
# ./gen_pagerank.exe <V> <E> <output_path> [seed] [damping] [tolerance] [max_iter]
```

## Run

```bash
./wrapper.exe
```


## Timing rule

For both algorithms, the timer starts immediately before the algorithm
call and stops immediately after. File reading, input validation, and
adjacency-list → CSR conversion (`build_csr`) all happen before the timer
starts and are excluded from the reported time.

## Input validation

- **Vertex Coloring**: rejects a self-loop, an out-of-range neighbour id,
  or an asymmetric edge (an edge listed at `u` but missing from `v`'s row).
- **PageRank**: rejects a non-positive or `>= 1` damping factor, a
  non-positive tolerance, or a non-positive `MAX_ITERATIONS`; also
  rejects malformed rows (declared outdegree not matching the neighbour
  count) or out-of-range vertex/neighbour ids.

## Algorithm notes

- **Vertex Coloring**: greedy Welsh-Powell — vertices ordered by
  non-increasing degree, each assigned the smallest color unused by any
  already-colored neighbour. Uses a stamped `forbidden_at[color] = v`
  array instead of clearing a fresh array per vertex, so the coloring
  pass runs in O(V + E) rather than O(V²).
- **PageRank**: standard power-iteration update with damping; dangling
  vertices (outdegree 0) distribute their rank evenly across all N
  vertices each iteration. Stops when total absolute rank change ≤
  `TOLERANCE` or `MAX_ITERATIONS` is reached.

## Results — Vertex Coloring

| File | V | E | Colors Used | Valid? | Time | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| color_10.txt | 10 | 20 | 4 | Yes | 0.0015 ms | Pass |
| color_100.txt | 100 | 250 | 5 | Yes | 0.0077 ms | Pass |
| color_10000.txt | 10,000 | 25,000 | 6 | Yes | 0.71 ms | Pass |
| color_50000.txt | 50,000 | 125,000 | 6 | Yes | 4.14 ms | Pass |
| color_100000.txt | 100,000 | 250,000 | 6 | Yes | 8.55 ms | Pass |

(`color_example_spec.txt` holds the 5-vertex worked example from the
assignment sheet, kept for verification, not counted as a required-size
test.)

## Results — PageRank

Damping 0.85, tolerance 1e-4, max iterations 100 for all files below.

| File | V | E | Top Vertex | Sum of Ranks | Iter. / Time | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| pagerank_10.txt | 10 | 20 | 0 | 1.000000 | 12 / 0.0014 ms | Pass |
| pagerank_100.txt | 100 | 250 | 99 | 1.000000 | 33 / 0.0128 ms | Pass |
| pagerank_1000.txt | 1,000 | 3,000 | 653 | 1.000000 | 15 / 0.0882 ms | Pass |
| pagerank_10000.txt | 10,000 | 30,000 | 193 | 1.000000 | 15 / 1.83 ms | Pass |
| pagerank_50000.txt | 50,000 | 150,000 | 48,861 | 1.000000 | 15 / 9.86 ms | Pass |

100,000-vertex PageRank is optional per the spec and was not generated;
`gen_pagerank.exe 100000 300000 tests/pagerank_100000.txt` produces it on
demand. (`pagerank_example_spec.txt` holds the 4-vertex worked example
from the assignment sheet.)

## Test-graph generation

- Vertex Coloring graphs: random, undirected, unweighted, no self-loops
  or parallel edges, kept sparse (E ≈ 2–2.5V in the tests above).
- PageRank graphs: random, directed, unweighted; dangling vertices
  (outdegree 0) occur naturally from the random draw and are handled by
  the algorithm's even-distribution rule.

